---
import PageHeader from '@/components/PageHeader.astro';
import { site } from '@/config/site';
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description={`About ${site.name}: how the site works, where the maps come from, and how to contribute.`}>
  <PageHeader title="About" />
  <div class="container">
    <div class="prose about">
      <h2>Using the notes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Highlighted quotations</strong> are sources you should be able to recognise and use. Click one to see who said it and why it matters.</li>
        <li><strong>Underlined key terms</strong> open a card with a definition and their significance — the point a strong exam answer makes.</li>
        <li><strong>Historians' debate</strong> sections summarise interpretations you can use in Paper 2 and 3 essays.</li>
        <li><strong>Test yourself</strong> questions at the end of each topic hide their answers until you ask.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The notes support your class, not replace it. Your teacher's course outline and the current IB History guide are
        the final word on what you need to know.
      </p>

      <h2>The 2028 course</h2>
      <p>
        Current notes follow the revised IB History course, first assessed in 2028: political and economic transitions
        (Paper 1), authoritarian rule (Paper 2) and, at HL, Europe — the French Revolution and the unification of Germany
        and Italy (Paper 3). Earlier syllabus material is labelled as an archive.
      </p>

      <h2>Maps</h2>
      <p>
        Historical borders come from the open
        <a href="https://github.com/aourednik/historical-basemaps">historical-basemaps</a> project by André Ourednik and
        contributors (GPL-3.0), simplified and with some anachronistic names corrected. Borders before 1800 are especially
        approximate; approximate borders are drawn dashed. Land shapes are from
        <a href="https://www.naturalearthdata.com/">Natural Earth</a> (public domain); the globe is rendered with
        <a href="https://maplibre.org/">MapLibre GL</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Contributing</h2>
      <p>
        Every topic, term, teacher profile and news post is a single text file. The
        <a href={site.repo}>source repository</a> explains how to add one — start with <code>AGENTS.md</code>. The site
        updates a minute or two after a change is merged.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about {
    padding-bottom: clamp(48px, 7vw, 96px);
  }
</style>
